### LeadLens API - open in VS Code with the "REST Client" extension and click "Send Request".
### Start the app first: npm run dev

@base = http://localhost:3000/api

### 1. Create a lead (inserted as pending, analysed, returned). Takes a few seconds.
# @name createLead
POST {{base}}/leads
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Riya Sharma",
  "location": "Sector 62, Noida",
  "property_requirement": "3BHK apartment, high floor, near metro",
  "budget": "1.4-1.5 Cr, home loan pre-approved",
  "timeline": "within_1_month",
  "message": "Hi, we saw a 3BHK in Sector 62 and also have an offer on another flat that expires Friday. Can we visit this weekend? Is there parking for 2 cars?",
  "contact": "riya@example.com"
}

### The id of the lead created above (used by the requests below)
@leadId = {{createLead.response.body.id}}

### 2. List leads (score desc, newest first)
GET {{base}}/leads

### 3. Get one lead
GET {{base}}/leads/{{leadId}}

### 4. Chat about this lead (streams a reply grounded in the lead)
POST {{base}}/leads/{{leadId}}/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{ "text": "What should I emphasize on the call?" }

### 5. Chat history (oldest first) - should contain the question and the answer from step 4
GET {{base}}/leads/{{leadId}}/messages

### 6. Re-analyse. Send it twice quickly: the second one returns 409 (already analysing).
POST {{base}}/leads/{{leadId}}/reanalyze

### 7. Delete. Returns 403 unless ENABLE_DELETE=true in .env.local.
DELETE {{base}}/leads/{{leadId}}

### 8a. Add the 6 sample leads (returns them as pending + queued; the dashboard button also analyses them)
POST {{base}}/leads/seed

### 8b. Property matches for the lead (computed in code, no AI)
GET {{base}}/leads/{{leadId}}/matches

### 8c. Ask the AI to explain and compare those matches (429 if repeated within 60 s)
POST {{base}}/leads/{{leadId}}/matches

### 8d. Call prep: generate (429 if repeated within 60 s)
POST {{base}}/leads/{{leadId}}/call-prep

### 8e. Call prep: tick questions 0 and 2
PATCH {{base}}/leads/{{leadId}}/call-prep
Content-Type: application/json

{ "asked": [0, 2] }

### --- Error cases ---

### 8. Validation error -> 400 with fieldErrors
POST {{base}}/leads
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "", "timeline": "soon" }

### 9. Unknown or malformed id -> 404
GET {{base}}/leads/not-a-real-id

### 10. Empty chat message -> 400
POST {{base}}/leads/{{leadId}}/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{ "text": "   " }
